# Strategy: SURGICAL ADD ONLY (do NOT touch any build #5 mark_debug)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Build #5 fixes the master FCSM-stuck-at-7 surface (L8 fix) but V1's
# diagnosis predicts the slave RX FIFO still stays empty because the slave
# RX framer NACK-worthy-decodes the master's packet → latches send_nack_req
# → bounces FCSM back to state 4. The signals below resolve which branch
# of the decode predicate trips (was the packet seen as a data pkt? was the
# packet number not the expected one? did CRC fail? did the L7 forgive gate
# actually re-arm?).
#
# All probes are added INSIDE WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v at their existing
# wire/reg declarations. No new ports, no observer aliases, no Wlink.v
# changes. Vivado's mark_debug on a Verilog wire declaration is preserved
# through the local_overrides → flist path because the override file is
# read instead of the upstream Wlink.v (same as the build #4/#5 LL_RX
# probes already in tree).
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Probe set — 8 net-bits total (well under the 30-bit headroom)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  File: src/rtl/local_overrides/WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v
#
#  Line  Signal                       Bits  Clock        Risk  Why
#  284   pkt_is_data_pkt              1     io_rx_clk    LOW   "is the master pkt being decoded as a data pkt at all?" — V1 Bug A predicate. Pure combinational wire of (sop & valid & data_id==swi_data_id_1 & ~crc_corrupt). hclk-asynchronous but native to io_rx_clk just like llrx_io_obs_valid (already mark_debug'd).
#  318   isExpPacket                  1     io_tx_clk    LOW   FIFO-side predicate — was the packet pulled out of the rx→tx hand-off FIFO classified as the expected pktnum? Pure combinational wire of ack_nack_fifo_io_rdata[18:16] decode.
#  402   _T_54                        1     io_tx_clk    LOW   FCSM byte counter == 0 — gates state transitions out of LINK_DATA back to 4. V1 calls this out as the FCSM decode predicate; pure combinational wire of `count` reg.
#  322   crcCorruptSeen               1     io_tx_clk    LOW   FIFO-side classified-as-CRC-corrupt — one of the two drivers that re-arms send_nack_req in steady state. Combinational wire of FIFO rdata decode.
#  387   isNotExpPacket_l7            1     io_tx_clk    LOW   The other steady-state driver — combinational mask of isNotExpPacket gated by the L7 forgive bit. If this stays high in steady state, the L7 fix didn't fully suppress the bringup transient.
#  366   send_nack_req                1     io_tx_clk    LOW   The signal that pushes the slave FCSM into state==7 and bounces back to 4. NOT SW-managed, NOT CDC-crossed-into-pclk — same domain as `state` (already mark_debug'd). io_tx_clk reg.
#  380   socl_l7_reached_link_data    1     io_tx_clk    LOW   L7 sticky witness — once state==5 is observed it latches and disarms the forgive gate. Confirms whether bringup ever reached LINK_DATA on this side.
#  381   socl_l7_bringup_forgive      1     io_tx_clk    LOW   Combinational gate that nulls send_nack_req in all states. Probing this confirms whether the L7 fix is active when send_nack_req re-arms.
#
#  Total: 8 net-bits added. No removals. Build #5 probe set kept verbatim.
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Risk classification
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   LOW  (top-scope or clock-native wire — no fold hazard)
#     All 8 probes. They are pure combinational wires (5) or regs (3) sitting
#     in the same clock domain as already-mark_debug'd FCSM state. No CDC
#     crossing, no SW-managed APB regs, no returner-busy-clear path, no
#     pclk/hclk handshake. Closest precedent: the existing
#     tl2wl_io_obs_pkt_is_cr_pkt / pkt_is_crack_pkt mark_debug aliases in
#     Wlink.v:252-253 — those are siblings of pkt_is_data_pkt in the same
#     FCSM scope, mark_debug, and build #4 did NOT regress on those.
#
#   MEDIUM (pclk/hclk reg potentially folding with build #5 set)
#     None.
#
#   HIGH  (SW-managed / returner busy-clear / known build #4 R-1 class)
#     None. Specifically AVOIDED:
#       - pair_credit_counter (build #5 already removes this)
#       - any returner_busy or skid path
#       - any APB read-mux path
#       - any pclk-domain reg
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Probes NOT included (deliberately — under V1 spec but absent in RTL)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#   - `send_nack_req_pending` — V1's spec named this signal but it does NOT
#     exist in WlinkGenericFCSM_6.v under that name. The actual path that
#     pushes the slave back to state 4 is `send_nack_req` itself (the
#     io_tx_clk reg at :366) which transitions state→7→4. We probe that
#     reg directly — the "_pending" suffix V1 invoked corresponds to the
#     reg's pre-clock value but Vivado captures the reg output anyway.
#
#   - Sticky-on-(valid && data_id==0xa1) version of pkt_is_data_pkt — V1's
#     description was approximate; in the actual Verilog the signal is
#     combinational (line 284), not sticky. The combinational version is
#     what feeds the FCSM and the FIFO write enable, so probing the live
#     wire is correct.
#
#   - `_T_54` in WlinkRxLinkLayer.v (line 911) — distinct signal, 17-bit
#     byte_count + 4 arithmetic; collides in Chisel name but is unrelated
#     to the FCSM decode predicate. NOT probed.
